{
  "engine": "front-end-with-html",
  "graderHint": "validateApplication",
  "flagsHint": "detectFlaggedIssues",
  "flagsArgs": [
    "state"
  ],
  "note": "validateApplication(a) returns only { eligibilityClass, countedAdults, indicativeOutcome } with no rules array and no flags, so this is a SPLIT engine: the oracle pins detectFlaggedIssues(state) as expected.flaggedIssues with flagsArgs [\"state\"], mirroring form-app.js. Classification is first-match: any disqualifier -> likely-ineligible (indicativeOutcome 'none'); any missing item -> incomplete; else likely-eligible. Counted adults are the applicant plus roster occupants whose status is '' or 'counted-adult'; the roster is ignored when household.othersLive is 'no'. The 'timestamp' and 'reasons' keys are added by form-app.js, not the grader. Eligibility is decided by the billing authority. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas united-kingdom-council-tax-discount-application --update",
